<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila stock exchange stops Cebu Shipyard surge.</title>
<headline>Manila stock exchange stops Cebu Shipyard surge.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philipine Stock Exchange (PSE) froze the share price of Cebu Shipyard &amp; Engineering Works Inc on Thursday after the issue hit the 50 percent price hike ceiling.</p>
<p>The stock exchange stopped the rise of Cebu Shipyard when the issue rose from one peso to 1.50 peso or by 50 percent.</p>
<p>Trading volume, however, was thin at 10,000 shares.</p>
<p>Cebu Shipyard is a unit of Keppel Philippines Holdings Inc, the local flagship of Singapore's Keppel Corp Ltd.</p>
<p>The PSE has asked the company to explain the rise in its A shares.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418939 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
